    <ID>MayBeConstant:TaoMainDispatcher.kt:TaoMainDispatcher$/** * Re-arm throttle. When a pumped block re-dispatches itself synchronously * (very common with Compose's state-observer / snapshot-apply machinery — * `LazyColumn` + scrollbar can cycle through ~150 k pumps/sec at idle), * the pump→drain→re-arm→nativeWake→pump loop pegs the Tao main thread * at 100 % CPU. AWT-based backends don't see this because the EDT only * processes pending work at ~60 Hz; we mimic that here by deferring the * re-arm `nativeWake` through a small delay rather than calling it * synchronously inside [pump]. New external dispatches still wake the * loop immediately — the delay only applies when the queue is non-empty * *after* a drain (i.e. blocks added by the just-run blocks). */ private val pumpReArmIntervalNs = 1_000_000_000L / 60</ID>
